{"title":"2015 AIME II Problems/Problem 13","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Clearer_Explanation_for_the_End\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Clearer Explanation for the End</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Define the sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/a/c4a82e7c7dbf7b035a66b5890ec80463b4c3e8d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1, a_2, a_3, \\ldots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"98\" height=\"13\" /> by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/0/7b0b99322612a80b3f24176bc81dfffa51642e45.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_n = \\sum\\limits_{k=1}^n \\sin{k}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"106\" height=\"48\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> represents radian measure. Find the index of the 100th term for which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/e/b2e64135fcfc3b060e2dff4ffd1ba37ad2757f98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_n &lt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/6/c766f9fce6070981e62f805a7cf7294baed4498e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/b/6eba281919715ad357b86d1c76555590f9b97472.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_n = \\sin(1) &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"121\" height=\"18\" />.  Then if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> satisfies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/e/b2e64135fcfc3b060e2dff4ffd1ba37ad2757f98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_n &lt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/7/317096889b84df0b72bf69ceb4c82208305f1b0f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\ge 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"46\" height=\"16\" />, and\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/9/96918761f5122666dcaee8069f8110f40c849195.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a_n = \\sum_{k=1}^n \\sin(k) = \\cfrac{1}{\\sin{1}} \\sum_{k=1}^n\\sin(1)\\sin(k) = \\cfrac{1}{2\\sin{1}} \\sum_{k=1}^n\\cos(k - 1) - \\cos(k + 1) = \\cfrac{1}{2\\sin(1)} [\\cos(0) + \\cos(1) - \\cos(n) - \\cos(n + 1)].\\]\" width=\"924\" height=\"48\" />\nSince <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/8/f983da9fa2b1165939e68cdb77b57af9d655634f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\sin 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"45\" height=\"12\" /> is positive, it does not affect the sign of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/1/6f1a2b6b7c193f9ba2b2134a59f1da5addcfbc98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"20\" height=\"13\" />.  Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/b/b0b95bddf9e5fa6116b1a9f6619d63871ec84405.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_n = \\cos(0) + \\cos(1) - \\cos(n) - \\cos(n + 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"331\" height=\"18\" />.  Now since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/0/ba05dc0e9842325f902012c14a60ca3db2863cc2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos(0) + \\cos(1) = 2\\cos\\left(\\cfrac{1}{2}\\right)\\cos\\left(\\cfrac{1}{2}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"282\" height=\"43\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/4/944bf88df8a9089e1ea11ef2dc034312cd462c84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos(n) + \\cos(n + 1) = 2\\cos\\left(n + \\cfrac{1}{2}\\right)\\cos\\left(\\cfrac{1}{2}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"350\" height=\"43\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/f/8ffd01cdc48042ce7c67d8edcd4904809831cfe4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" /> is negative if and only if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/3/69381db3d29cad3d377546043b17229c1784c8a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos\\left(\\cfrac{1}{2}\\right) &lt; \\cos\\left(n + \\cfrac{1}{2}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"183\" height=\"43\" />, or when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/a/aca3a393a9fcb4cb635edf001fdad87d99855347.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\in [2k\\pi - 1, 2k\\pi]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"145\" height=\"20\" />.  Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/c/f2ca003a7da0de4994b4733e203b74ff52d42553.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pi$\" width=\"10\" height=\"8\" /> is irrational, there is always only one integer in the range, so there are values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/e/b2e64135fcfc3b060e2dff4ffd1ba37ad2757f98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_n &lt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"15\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/6/766d2ae5b434179cf083b7e7ec27a9d636335399.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\pi, 4\\pi, \\cdots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"76\" height=\"15\" />.  Then the hundredth such value will be when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/0/200cbb3a9b14cedb386e2445dc580af6dfc67c32.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k = 100$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"61\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/6/7c600a8eca9dfef7b0a49140e11dde24ec376e87.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = \\lfloor 200\\pi \\rfloor = \\lfloor 628.318 \\rfloor = \\boxed{628}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"253\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Clearer_Explanation_for_the_End\">Clearer Explanation for the End</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Clearer Explanation for the End\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Notice that we want <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/7/4d74f9a0d3b69074ba3ea81ee49b8e67b11ea09b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos(n+1/2)&gt;\\cos(1/2).$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"196\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Notice that the only interval in which this is true, is where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/d/cad774a0255e38dbf183d574e279da61b591740c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-1/2 &lt; n + 1/2 &lt; 1/2.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"184\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Thus, we need <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/5/5d565f814c297cfe7743ec11040fdaee107c0165.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-1&lt;n&lt;0.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"99\" height=\"15\" /> So we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/d/e2d3bb9407e2605f20d5730955dbcdc33093535a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-1+2\\pi k &lt;n &lt;0+2\\pi k.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"203\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>But we want the 100th solution. Which means <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is in between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/b/f5b158a6bf4b89b3368a3956d8c8aff64f98c897.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$200\\pi - 1 &lt; n &lt; 200 \\pi.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"174\" height=\"15\" /> So n = 628.\n</p><p>~mathboy282\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Notice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/1/6f1a2b6b7c193f9ba2b2134a59f1da5addcfbc98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"20\" height=\"13\" /> is the imaginary part of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/e/38e8991d7a12b43018a7e6e91cdfd7cac339b2a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{k=1}^n e^{ik}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"48\" height=\"48\" />, by Euler's formula. Using the geometric series formula, we find that this sum is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/1/6f1ff6f0c8c237076e7063b014d7f74e6476a452.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{e^{i(n+1)}-e^i}{e^i-1} = \\frac{\\cos (n+1) - \\cos 1 + i (\\sin (n+1) - \\sin 1) }{\\cos 1 - 1 + i \\sin 1}\\]\" width=\"431\" height=\"41\" /> We multiply the fraction by the conjugate of the denominator so that we can separate out the real and imaginary parts of the above expression. Multiplying, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/2/452c6fb436647eec15723e6c5539206680eef2d8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{(\\cos 1 - 1)(\\cos(n+1)-\\cos 1) + (\\sin 1)(\\sin(n+1)-\\sin 1) + i((\\sin(n+1) - \\sin 1)(\\cos 1 - 1) - (\\sin 1)(\\cos(n+1)-\\cos 1))}{\\cos^2 1 - 2 \\cos 1 + 1 + \\sin^2 1}\\]\" width=\"954\" height=\"41\" /> We only need to look at the imaginary part, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/8/d4866c26c0d283a39cd3423915cb33f84f165d1c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{(\\sin(n+1) \\cos 1 - \\cos(n+1) \\sin 1) - \\sin 1 \\cos 1 + \\sin 1 - \\sin (n+1) + \\sin 1 \\cos 1}{2-2 \\cos 1} = \\frac{\\sin n - \\sin(n+1) + \\sin 1}{2-2 \\cos 1}\\]\" width=\"845\" height=\"39\" />\nSince <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/0/650023e2c2d3a73490134473a84e1cc395f1a56a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos 1 &lt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"68\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/1/bf1c441f05423f03130caf4906462f8e39b5bf0d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2-2 \\cos 1 &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"112\" height=\"13\" />, so the denominator is positive. Thus, in order for the whole fraction to be negative, we must have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/9/bf954e8d1e63a2c7215f98326f3ed4af1fcc3bcf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin (n+1) - \\sin n &gt; \\sin 1 \\implies 2 \\cos \\left(n + \\frac{1}{2} \\right) \\sin \\frac{1}{2} &gt; \\sin 1 \\implies \\cos \\left( n + \\frac{1}{2} \\right) &gt; \\frac{\\sin 1}{2 \\sin{\\frac{1}{2}}} = \\cos \\left(\\frac{1}{2} \\right),$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"781\" height=\"45\" /> by sum to product. This only holds when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/5/91540fab193d4d0f123f5643163e8e39d946bb65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\pi k - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/e/7ae2c7a01e7156b3153ba1594d81824a9b87bc67.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\pi k$\" width=\"29\" height=\"12\" /> for integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> [continuity proof here], and since this has exactly one integer solution for every such interval, the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/9/e59e2c6e83eb78cca610a5fd4070ae01c8d4ae60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />th such <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/b/84b109064aa3c9318f1f46f7b0a8b7da64660156.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lfloor 200\\pi \\rfloor = \\boxed{628}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"119\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Similar to solution 2, we set a complex number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/2/c52b0591f3bcf7a3254afce03d758485b2f9f7b8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z=\\cos 1+i\\sin 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"135\" height=\"14\" />. We start from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> instead of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> starts from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />: be careful.\n</p><p>The sum of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/d/98dd8f1be007aad75004cb7d02beda5d42cd985d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z+z^2+z^3+z^4+z^5\\dots=\\frac{z-z^{n+1}}{1-z}=\\frac{z}{z-1}\\left(z^n-1\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"418\" height=\"39\" />.\n</p><p>We are trying to make <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> so that the imaginary part of this expression is negative.\n</p><p>The argument of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. The argument of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/e/50e0412f1e4c5bde18c5a76f43bd0c5256c8fb2a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"39\" height=\"12\" />, however, is a little more tricky. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/e/50e0412f1e4c5bde18c5a76f43bd0c5256c8fb2a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"39\" height=\"12\" /> is on a circle centered on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/b/c9b83617178c137c55232eea1ca6791131d94eca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(-1,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"56\" height=\"20\" /> with radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. The change in angle due to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> with respect to the center, but the angle that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/e/50e0412f1e4c5bde18c5a76f43bd0c5256c8fb2a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"39\" height=\"12\" /> makes with the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />-axis is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/1/411f9bf1e8e835e843cb192785adb12099f885e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$half$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"36\" height=\"16\" /> the change, due to Circle Theorems (this intercepted arc is the argument of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />), because the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />- axis is tangent to the circle at the origin. So <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/f/cbf79927d7ba65337a1ba610809e2d253c02639f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{arg}(z-1)=\\frac{\\pi+1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"146\" height=\"37\" />. Dividing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/e/50e0412f1e4c5bde18c5a76f43bd0c5256c8fb2a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"39\" height=\"12\" /> subtracts the latter argument from the former, so the angle of the quotient with the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />-axis is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/e/d2e6fcae0ab96410b534ed0ccfb901d0f435c9ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1-\\pi}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"44\" height=\"37\" />. \n</p><p>We want the argument of the whole expression <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/f/25f7595b1c895c4ee26368b57f45919481b1d236.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-\\pi&lt;\\theta&lt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"91\" height=\"13\" />. This translates into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/4/c64b89a8c606e3d5f03596eb89553ade3058961e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{-\\pi-1}{2}&lt;\\text{arg}\\left(z^n-1\\right)&lt;\\frac{\\pi-1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"243\" height=\"37\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/9/119e73aee0a7fb6dc2237809ffc5025473397cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z^n-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"48\" height=\"13\" /> also consists of points on the circle centered at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/b/c9b83617178c137c55232eea1ca6791131d94eca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(-1,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"56\" height=\"20\" />, so we deal with this argument similarly: the argument of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/9/689a869366b7bce0801a72fdd707a065315ba0ce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z^n$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> is twice the angle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/9/119e73aee0a7fb6dc2237809ffc5025473397cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z^n-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"48\" height=\"13\" /> makes with the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />-axis. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/9/119e73aee0a7fb6dc2237809ffc5025473397cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z^n-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"48\" height=\"13\" /> is always negative, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/2/762caec351c1b0e1c467f8172602199aafe5488c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{-3\\pi}{2}&lt;\\text{arg}\\left(z^n-1\\right)&lt;\\frac{-\\pi}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"204\" height=\"37\" />, and the left bound is the only one that is important. Either way, the line (the line consists of both bounds) makes a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/3/193e9126c14d0ba4a6d7c9c823309130fadb3e8b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\pi}{2}-\\frac{\\pi-1}{2}=\\frac{-1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"133\" height=\"37\" /> angle with the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />-axis both ways.\n</p><p>So the argument of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/9/689a869366b7bce0801a72fdd707a065315ba0ce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z^n$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> must be in the bound <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/c/9ec01ff3baa1e464b7a7144f7a34c0dbe36ec30a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-1&lt;\\theta&lt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"89\" height=\"13\" /> by doubling, namely the last <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/9/689a869366b7bce0801a72fdd707a065315ba0ce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z^n$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> negative before another rotation. Since there is always one <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/9/689a869366b7bce0801a72fdd707a065315ba0ce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z^n$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> in this category per rotation because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/c/f2ca003a7da0de4994b4733e203b74ff52d42553.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pi$\" width=\"10\" height=\"8\" /> is irrational, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/3/2838f0cc401c6622231e67e28c09516b2c619153.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n_{100}\\equiv z^{628}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"84\" height=\"17\" /> and the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/7/167c0e9424423dc6153547669ec296fd3c30acb8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{628}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>By the product-to-sum formula,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/4/ca4f825d8b4e3c18862dc96280fa470570fceb21.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sin \\frac{1}{2} \\sin k = \\frac{1}{2} \\left[ \\cos \\left( k - \\frac{1}{2} \\right) - \\cos \\left( k + \\frac{1}{2} \\right) \\right].\\]\" width=\"362\" height=\"43\" />Thus, we can make the sum in the problem telescope:\n\\begin{align*}\na_n &amp;= \\sum_{k = 1}^n \\sin k \\\\\n&amp;= \\sum_{k = 1}^n \\frac{\\sin \\frac{1}{2} \\sin k}{\\sin \\frac{1}{2}} \\\\\n&amp;= \\sum_{k = 1}^n \\frac{\\cos (k - \\frac{1}{2}) - \\cos (k + \\frac{1}{2})}{2 \\sin \\frac{1}{2}} \\\\\n&amp;= \\frac{(\\cos \\frac{1}{2} - \\cos \\frac{3}{2}) + (\\cos \\frac{3}{2} - \\cos \\frac{5}{2}) + \\dots + (\\cos \\frac{2n - 1}{2} - \\cos \\frac{2n + 1}{2})}{2 \\sin \\frac{1}{2}} \\\\\n&amp;= \\frac{\\cos \\frac{1}{2} - \\cos \\frac{2n + 1}{2}}{2 \\sin \\frac{1}{2}}.\n\\end{align*}Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/e/b2e64135fcfc3b060e2dff4ffd1ba37ad2757f98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_n &lt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"15\" /> when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/e/40e79361a066621a6d0042206a404dc153ea539f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos \\frac{1}{2} &lt; \\cos \\frac{2n + 1}{2}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"154\" height=\"38\" /> This occurs if and only if\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/b/aabdc1a01f07e5f3e3f96c2139b7dc9b0f2675ed.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2 \\pi k - \\frac{1}{2} &lt; \\frac{2n + 1}{2} &lt; 2 \\pi k + \\frac{1}{2}\\]\" width=\"232\" height=\"37\" />for some integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/4/5d48e0968a64d782fe75bca620ce749938b7d0bb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k.$\" width=\"13\" height=\"12\" /> Equivalently,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/9/6895760d366a7ecc731394f891e719fa91d2776f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2 \\pi k - 1 &lt; n &lt; 2 \\pi k.\\]\" width=\"154\" height=\"13\" />In other words, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/d/57d8b4a029e059e1480793923489300ff6e9727a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = \\lfloor 2 \\pi k \\rfloor.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"88\" height=\"20\" /> The 100th index of this form is then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/1/11160d883e97d8d0704b6072073a0ed7d5dd7c1b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lfloor 2 \\pi \\cdot 100 \\rfloor = \\boxed{628}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"146\" height=\"25\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/b1-cUUPjYNk\">https://youtu.be/b1-cUUPjYNk</a>\n</p><p>~MathProblemSolvingSkills\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_II\" title=\"2015 AIME II\">2015 AIME II</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_II_Problems\" title=\"2015 AIME II Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_II_Answer_Key\" title=\"2015 AIME II Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2015\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2015 AIME II Problems/Problem 12\">Problem 12</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2015 AIME II Problems/Problem 14\">Problem 14</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2015 AIME II Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2015 AIME II Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2015 AIME II Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2015 AIME II Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2015 AIME II Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2015 AIME II Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2015 AIME II Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2015 AIME II Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2015 AIME II Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2015 AIME II Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2015 AIME II Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2015 AIME II Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2015 AIME II Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2015 AIME II Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\"> All AIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017102539\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.061 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.090 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 570/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1810/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 132/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 18424/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   14.087      1 -total\n 61.66%    8.686      1 Template:AIME_box\n 36.78%    5.181      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:14142:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017102539 and revision id 221843. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}